{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02927",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 6.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat. What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.17,
      "end_seconds": 24.56,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, I've been dealing with severe pain in my left side going to the groin. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.56,
      "end_seconds": 33.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.6,
      "end_seconds": 36.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Probably two days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.34,
      "end_seconds": 43.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.49,
      "end_seconds": 56.87,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "Right, a three out of ten, I suppose. It happens a couple of times a week. I get some relief from heat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.19,
      "end_seconds": 64.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.01,
      "end_seconds": 77.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.49,
      "text": "It usually comes with blood in the urine. Yeah, the blood in the urine? That's been since last weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.11,
      "end_seconds": 80.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.5,
      "end_seconds": 89.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.19,
      "end_seconds": 111.14,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 124 over 72, height 178 centimetres, heart rate 74, weight 97 kilos, temperature is 36.7 degrees, respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.65,
      "end_seconds": 115.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.97,
      "end_seconds": 122.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.65,
      "end_seconds": 126.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.49,
      "end_seconds": 143.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "You are writhing in pain with tenderness in the left loin but your tummy is soft."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.76,
      "end_seconds": 156.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "You can relax now. Did you get vomiting, burning when passing urine, passing no urine or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.88,
      "end_seconds": 160.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.72,
      "end_seconds": 165.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.31,
      "end_seconds": 168.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.67,
      "end_seconds": 175.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.26,
      "end_seconds": 180.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.08,
      "end_seconds": 184.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.68,
      "end_seconds": 204.57,
      "duration_seconds": 17.89,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I look after my grandchildren most days. No, I share a house with my brother. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.65,
      "end_seconds": 227.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "So, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.63,
      "end_seconds": 233.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.54,
      "end_seconds": 235.24,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.64,
      "end_seconds": 250.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.34,
      "end_seconds": 255.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I take warfarin, 3 milligrams, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.53,
      "end_seconds": 280.13,
      "duration_seconds": 13.6,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards kidney stone colic. Another possibility is a urine infection. I want a CT scan of the kidneys and bladder done, that's for renal colic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.55,
      "end_seconds": 283.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Mm, um, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.8,
      "end_seconds": 296.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.9,
      "text": "For this, diclofenac, 75 milligrams, once now, single dose. It's for renal colic. Drink plenty of water and strain the urine to catch the stone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.92,
      "end_seconds": 312.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.77,
      "text": "Yes. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in one week. Okay, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.79,
      "end_seconds": 327.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.5,
      "text": "So, I take the diclofenac, 75 milligrams, once now and come back in one week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.06,
      "end_seconds": 333.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.44,
      "end_seconds": 338.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.48,
      "end_seconds": 341.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}